# READ-FIELD-CLOSURE (T7), a bare free name in a callable merge's node takes the caller's binding first: model's local
# S reads cnt, a free name model forwards as its hidden input.  The root's own cnt is 9 (its write), the unit's cell
# 11 (poke's explicit write after the root's own), the copy made at the merge 7; w() gives the caller's 9, neither the
# graph cell nor the copied lexical value -- a lexical context copied by merge is only the fallback (docs #dynamic).
# Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
int: cnt 7
fn: model (int: y) int
    S:
        int: v 0
        v: cnt
    S
    return: S\v
fn: wrap (int: k) fn: () int
    return: merge(y: k; model)
sub: poke ()
    node\cnt: 11
@: w wrap(5)
cnt: 9
poke()
int: result w()
int: ok 7
if: result != 9
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
